==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|ka-blooey|ka-blooie}}
* {{alter|en|kablooey}}
* {{alter|en|kerblooey|kerblooie|kerplooie}}

===Etymology===
[[ka-]], an [[intensifier]] used with onomatopoeia, plus (probably) an imaginative rendition of an explosion or splash.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/kəˈbluːi/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-kablooie.ogg|a=US}}

===Interjection===
{{en-intj}}

# {{lb|en|colloquial}} A [[failure]], [[meltdown]]; or [[explosion]]; a [[splat]] or [[splash]].
#: {{coi|en|to go '''kablooie'''}}
#: {{coi|en|it went '''kablooie'''}}
#: {{ux|en|The bottle of ketchup hit the floor and went '''kablooie''' all over everything.}}

